{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/702","id":4732739493,"node_id":"PR_kwDORnQJEs8AAAABGhffpQ","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/702","diff_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/702.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pull/702.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/issues/702","number":702,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"test(checkout): #661 round 7 boundary tests","user":{"login":"BradleyGleavePortfolio","id":264851314,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8lPcg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264851314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> **Status (2026-10-05, fix round 2).** Tests-only PR stacked on #661 (base `agent/clinic/b-secrets-3`). Head `b96611de` merges #661 fix round 9 (`e0cc97e1`) and adds its regression and backfill tests (Sol B-661-14 / Opus B-661-15, C-661-2). It also carries the #661 round-7 tests (Sol B-661-3) and `test/checkout-hosted-activation-once.spec.ts`, moved here byte-identical by OP-SIZE-118 (#661 fix round 8, #702 fix round 1) to keep #661 under its 3,000-line ceiling. Lands with #661 as one unit (guide rule 11); never retarget it to main on its own. Needs both lenses at its exact head. Do not merge without audit.\n\n**Tier:** T4.\n**Why:** Money, entitlement and stored payment credentials: the tests prove that a paid one-time purchase whose payment failed and then succeeded gets its access back however many never-activated purchases share its PaymentIntent (#661 round 7), that a hosted session activates once (moved spec), and that a native subscription's first grant erases the spent PaymentSheet credentials while every payable attempt keeps them, plus the C-661-2 backfill (#661 round 9). Tests only; no source, schema, workflow or dependency change.\n**T4 trigger scan:** payments/Stripe data path: tests only (real `CheckoutWebhookHandlerService`, `CheckoutService`, `PurchaseFanoutService` and Prisma on real PostgreSQL; Stripe is a test double). Auth/tenancy: NO. Schema/migration: NO. New env name: NO. Workflow, `scripts/ci/*`, branch protection: NO (the spec is already in the `mwb-3-live-tests` list). Logging/redaction: NO.\n**T3 trigger scan:** none (no contract or shared primitive changes).\n**Bounded T1:** none.\n**Canonical builder:** agent 117 (B-661-R7-117); fix round 1: operator agent 118 (OP-SIZE-118); restack: agent 119 (B-661R-119); fix round 2: agent 120 (B-661R2-120).\n**Parent owner:** #661 (`agent/clinic/b-secrets-3`), fix round 9 at `e0cc97e150384d049823327b274ac47511ee952e`.\n**Acceptance evidence:** Fix round 2 (#661 round 9): `test/checkout-grant-credentials.spec.ts` (new, build-and-test; the real handler on the recurring fakes): `invoice.paid` and `customer.subscription.updated` grants (first invoice paid, own trial card saved by either event, a declined first attempt then paid) erase both credentials, one fanout; trials without a saved card (no default; a default with the create-time end still set) and an unpaid first invoice keep them; the conflict-resolved end erases on a paid plan and a carded trial (H1a, H1d). New block `#661 credentials at rest on real PostgreSQL` in `test/checkout-settlement.live.spec.ts` (`mwb-3-live-tests`; real handler, `PurchaseFanoutService`, Prisma): the four AUD-SOL-661D-120 acceptance cases, the unsaved-trial controls on both events, and the backfill over 13 spent, 6 payable and 1 credential-free rows (dry run writes nothing; batched `--apply` erases exactly the spent ones and nothing else; a rerun matches 0). Failing-before (src = #661 `bc399edd` + the script, handler fix absent): 9 failed / 20 passed, only the credential assertions, in [run 37348121187](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37348121187). After (this head plus both lenses' probes): 44 suites / 609 tests, `tsc --noEmit` green, in [run 37348700674](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37348700674). Round 7: `test/checkout-settlement.live.spec.ts` (+231 / -4 in round 7) runs in `mwb-3-live-tests` on real PostgreSQL with the full Prisma schema. New block `B-661-3 round 7: the owner query is complete at any number of adopted purchases`, `it.each([9, 10, 12])`: a hosted purchase (the owner) is created first; then `count` real native reservations are made through `CheckoutService.createPaymentIntentForClient` with the provider replies held, and each is adopted onto the owner's PaymentIntent by a real `payment_intent.payment_failed` delivery (metadata fallback) in its own held transaction; the owner's real `checkout.session.completed` activates it (one PurchaseFanout row, a deferred split), a real failure revokes it and cancels its drop, then the same PaymentIntent succeeds. Purchase reads that name no order are answered in an adversarial legal order (`legalOrder`: findMany newest first, findFirst oldest first). The test asserts the boundary itself (`count + 1` failed purchases on the PaymentIntent, exactly one activation record, an unfiltered ten-row read misses the owner from ten on), then: result `{ claimed: true, purchase_id: owner, reason: 'payment_recovered' }` (no second split descriptor), owner `paid` / entitled / `last_error` null, its drop pending again, every adopted purchase still `payment_failed` and unentitled with no activation record, exactly one PurchaseFanout row; after the held native replies land, every adopted purchase holds its own PaymentIntent and stays unentitled, and a redelivered success is `no_matching_purchase` with nothing changed. The existing live tests are unchanged (pool raised from 8 to 16 connections for the held transactions).\nFailing-before (these tests against #661 round 6 `c7ee15f0`, tests commit `617add10`): 2 failed / 31 passed, `tsc --noEmit` green, in [run 37186266591](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37186266591): the 10 and 12 cases return `{ claimed: false, reason: 'checkout_session_activates' }`; the 9 case (control) passes. After (this head's tree, #661 round 7 merged in): 190 / 190 across the live spec and the 11 affected unit suites, `tsc --noEmit` green, in [run 37186426457](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37186426457). The lane-only global setup that starts the runner's PostgreSQL is not in this PR.\n**Promotion triggers:** re-audit if `activatedFailedPurchases` stops filtering activation, one-time and subscription in the query, or if a PurchaseFanout row can be deleted while its purchase exists (it is the activation record).\n\n## What changed\n\n| Finding | Test | Before (#661 round 7 rows: c7ee15f0; round 9 rows: bc399edd) | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B-661-3 (Sol, round 6 verdict 5977638148): the owner lookup capped every failed row of the PaymentIntent at ten before checking activation | `B-661-3 round 7: ... behind %i never-activated purchases ...` (9, 10, 12) | 10 and 12 fail (`checkout_session_activates`), 9 passes | all pass |\n| B-661-14 (Sol) / B-661-15 (Opus): native first grant keeps the spent credentials | `checkout-grant-credentials.spec.ts` G1, G2, G3, G3b, G5; live block grant cases (4) | fail (credentials still held) | all pass |\n| controls (Sol lane 2, Opus G4) | G4 x2, G6; live unsaved-trial cases (2) | pass | pass |\n| C-661-15 (Opus): no test pins the resolved end | H1a, H1d | pass (behaviour from the conflict resolution) | pass |\n| C-661-2 backfill (operator ruling: include subscription rows) | live `C-661-2 backfill: ...` | script absent before round 9 | pass |\n\nAlso here since fix round 1 (OP-SIZE-118, comment 5982239336): `test/checkout-hosted-activation-once.spec.ts` (278 lines, the #661 round-4 hosted activation-once tests, byte-identical, SHA-256 `fc2e00c2...`; unchanged).\n\nSize: 831 changed lines (+826 / -5), all test, three files.\n","created_at":"2026-10-04T07:43:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T17:43:38Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d703fe27a8caf09fa7a23b66b46c810699cad079","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":11278565662,"node_id":"LA_kwDORnQJEs8AAAACoEFBHg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/labels/size/size/XL","name":"size/size/XL","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/702/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/702/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/issues/702/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.git